course: dictionary
lesson: 1379
title: Capillary: the tiniest tube
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: In science you will meet new words, and the words around them give clues. «Capillaries are the tiniest blood vessels; they reach almost every cell.» The words tiniest and reach almost every cell tell you that a capillary is a very small blood vessel found all over the body.
explain: «Arteries carry blood away from the heart, veins bring it back, and tiny capillaries join them inside every part of the body.» The word join is the clue. Capillaries link arteries and veins, so they are the bridge between them.
explain: Capillary can also be an adjective, as in capillary action. In the paper towel and celery experiments, water climbs up thin spaces by itself. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «capillary action» still makes sense as "the way water moves up thin tubes," you have it right.
fact: A capillary is the thinnest kind of blood vessel in the body, finer than a hair.
fact: Capillaries connect arteries and veins.
fact: Oxygen and food pass from capillaries into the body's cells.
fact: «Capillary» can also mean any very thin tube.
fact: Capillary action is the way water moves up through thin tubes or tiny gaps, like paper towels and celery, and it helps water rise in plants.
exercise: «Capillaries are the tiniest blood vessels; they reach almost every cell.» What are capillaries? | *The tiniest blood vessels in the body | The strongest muscles in the heart | The tubes that carry air to the lungs | The bones of the arm
exercise: «Arteries carry blood away from the heart, veins bring it back, and tiny capillaries join them.» Which two kinds of vessel do capillaries join? | Lungs and heart | Bones and muscles | Hair and skin | *Arteries and veins
exercise: In the paper towel experiment, water climbs up the paper by itself. What is this called? | *Capillary action | Evaporation | Photosynthesis | Digestion
test: What is the thinnest kind of blood vessel, finer than a hair? | Artery | Vein | *Capillary | Nerve
test: What does capillary action help to do in a plant? | Turn air into water | Pump blood to the leaves | *Move water up the stem | Make food from sunlight
exam: Which best describes capillary action? | Blood flowing fast out of the heart | Air rushing into the lungs | *Water moving up through thin tubes or tiny gaps | Food being broken down in the stomach
